{"humanId":"agent-mcp-003","kind":"agent","family":"agent-mcp","title":"claudecli provider silently discarded real token usage from the CLI's own result event","body":"packages/agent/agent-engine-orchestrator/src/providers/claudecli.ts drives the real `claude` binary via `-p --output-format stream-json`. The terminal `result` event on that stream already carries a fully-aggregated `usage` object (input_tokens/output_tokens/cache_read_input_tokens/cache_creation_input_tokens), plus total_cost_usd and a per-model modelUsage breakdown - computed by the CLI itself. But ClaudeStreamResultEvent only ever declared type/subtype/is_error/result, so `JSON.parse(line) as ClaudeStreamEvent` silently dropped the usage field on every claudecli-provider task. ProviderChatResponse.usage/rawUsage were never populated for this provider (unlike anthropic.ts/openai.ts, which do). Root cause traced via git history: commit b35075ee ("provider-neutral token accounting", BUG-ORCH-009/010) introduced usage/rawUsage/normaliseAnthropicUsage but its diff only touches anthropic.ts and openai.ts - claudecli.ts was never in scope for that effort, not a regression. Real-world effect: mcp__agent-mcp__usage_query recorded all-zero tokens (inputTokens:0, cacheReadTokens:null, stopReason:"unknown") for every claudecli-provider task, hiding real spend. Discovered and fixed while running a controlled dispatch-mechanism A/B test that needed real claudecli-provider cost data.

FIX APPLIED AND VERIFIED (already shipped, uncommitted in this working tree): patched claudecli.ts to declare usage/stop_reason/total_cost_usd on ClaudeStreamResultEvent, capture them when the result event fires, and populate ProviderChatResponse.usage/rawUsage via the existing normaliseAnthropicUsage - additive only, zero change to the CLI invocation/args. Verified three ways: (1) npx nx build agent-engine-orchestrator - clean; (2) npx nx test agent-engine-orchestrator - 88/88 pass including new claudecli-usage.test.ts (2 tests) with a real negative control (reverted the capture line, confirmed the test goes red, restored, confirmed green); (3) live end-to-end against the real built dist/ artifact and a real spawned claude -p subprocess (not mocked) - returned real non-zero usage. Then confirmed live through the FULL stack after a /mcp reload: dispatched a claudecli task before and after the reload and queried mcp__agent-mcp__usage_query directly - same result set shows the pre-reload task with zeros/stopReason:"unknown" and the post-reload task with real inputTokens:43042, cacheReadTokens:17507, cacheCreationTokens:25533, stopReason:"stop" side by side.

Not yet verified: whether the DB/schema layer this feeds into (task_usage grain, session/task/turn aggregation) matches what the active DEBT-AGENTMCP-ACCOUNTING-001 redesign in .worktrees/agent-mcp-usage-accounting expects - that worktree's changes were deliberately not touched by this fix since claudecli.ts was outside its modified-files list.","status":"FIXED","repo":"PseudoSky/adhd","citations":[{"file":"packages/agent/agent-engine-orchestrator/src/providers/claudecli.ts","context":"ClaudeStreamResultEvent + usage capture in chat()"},{"file":"packages/agent/agent-engine-orchestrator/src/__tests__/claudecli-usage.test.ts","context":"regression test with negative control"}],"notes":[{"by":"claude","at":"2026-07-25T02:03:18.748Z","text":"[transition to FIXED] Patched claudecli.ts to declare and capture the usage field already present on the CLI's terminal result event, populate ProviderChatResponse.usage/rawUsage via the existing normaliseAnthropicUsage. Verified: clean build, 88/88 tests pass (new claudecli-usage.test.ts with a real negative control), live end-to-end against the real built dist/ artifact and a real spawned claude -p subprocess, and confirmed through the full stack (provider -> engine -> task_usage DB -> usage_query) after a live /mcp reload - same usage_query result set shows the pre-fix task at zeros and the post-fix task with real inputTokens:43042/cacheReadTokens:17507/cacheCreationTokens:25533 side by side."},{"by":"claude","at":"2026-07-25T02:03:50.270Z","text":"Related: agent-mcp-001 (agent-mcp's anthropic/oauth provider has no credential path wired in .mcp.json) - discovered while investigating that item, but this is a genuinely distinct root cause/fix (claudecli usage capture, not credential wiring) and is now resolved independently. Note: mcp__backlog__backlog_client_d_link_related(agent-mcp-003, agent-mcp-001) was called but did not visibly take effect - the response was {"result":null} and agent-mcp-001's updatedAt was unchanged afterward, no related-items field appears on either item's get_item response. Adding this as a plain-text cross-reference since the structured link tool's success can't be confirmed. Worth its own small backlog note if link_related is silently a no-op."},{"by":"claude","at":"2026-08-20T21:13:12.981Z","text":"[repo migration] moved from repo="adhd" to repo="PseudoSky/adhd" — BUG-BACKLOG-REPO-SPLIT-001 / DEBT-BACKLOG-REPO-MOVE-001 reconciliation"}],"createdAt":"2026-07-25T02:03:09.249Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-20T21:13:12.981Z","priority":"MEDIUM","dedupeSymbol":"ClaudeStreamResultEvent","dedupePath":"packages/agent/agent-engine-orchestrator/src/providers/claudecli.ts"}

content:
Recommend: generalized model-string normalizer for rate-card lookups (fixes agent-mcp-005's root pattern, not just one table)

Companion to agent-mcp-005 (rate-card estimateCostUsd() returns null for every real model string). That item reports the symptom; this one recommends the actual fix and provides a concrete sample set to build/test against, since a narrow patch to RATE_CARD's keys alone will just recreate the same bug the next time a model ships.

PROBLEM PATTERN (confirmed twice independently in this session, in two unrelated codebases): a pricing/cost table keyed by one exact string format silently fails against the several DIFFERENT formats a model name actually appears in across a real system - bare alias, current canonical id, dated runtime snapshot id, and whatever ad-hoc key convention the table's author picked. scratch-claude-metadata (~/dev/ai/scratch/claude-metadata) hit and fixed the identical class of bug earlier the same day (agent_analytics.py's cost estimator) via a _split_model()/_resolve_family() normalization layer that resolves any input string down to a FAMILY (opus/sonnet/haiku/fable/mythos), then prices by family rather than by exact string match. Recommend the same architecture here: normalize-to-family, not exact-string-match.

RECOMMENDED SHAPE:
```ts
// packages/agent/agent-core-provider/src/pricing/normalize-model.ts
export function normalizeModelKey(raw: string): string | null {
  const s = raw.trim().toLowerCase();
  // 1. bare alias -> current canonical family
  const ALIASES: Record<string, string> = {
    haiku: 'claude_haiku_4_5', sonnet: 'claude_sonnet_4_6' /* or _5 once added, see below */,
    opus: 'claude_opus_4_8', fable: 'claude_fable_5', mythos: 'claude_fable_5',
  };
  if (ALIASES[s]) return ALIASES[s];
  // 2. strip a trailing dated snapshot suffix (8 digits) before matching, e.g.
  //    claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 -> claude-haiku-4-5
  const noDate = s.replace(/-\d{8}$/, '');
  // 3. hyphen -> underscore, since RATE_CARD's Claude keys are underscored
  //    (but its DeepSeek keys are hyphenated - pick ONE convention and migrate
  //    RATE_CARD to it rather than normalizing inputs two different ways)
  const key = noDate.replace(/-/g, '_');
  return key in RATE_CARD ? key : null; // still null (never 0) if truly unrecognized
}
```
Call this once at the top of estimateCostUsd() instead of the raw RATE_CARD[model] lookup. Keep the existing 'null, never 0, for a genuinely unknown model' behavior - the fix is making 'genuinely unknown' correctly rare instead of the default outcome.

FULL SAMPLE SET to build/test the normalizer against - grouped by source and confidence:

**Directly verified LIVE this session (highest confidence - actually observed on the wire):**
- `claude-haiku-4-5-20251001` -> should resolve to claude_haiku_4_5 (captured from a real `claude -p --output-format stream-json` result event AND from mcp__agent-mcp__usage_query's own `model` column for a real claudecli task)
- `claude-sonnet-5` -> should resolve to whatever the Sonnet-5 rate-card key becomes (seen in real usage_query rows this session; note RATE_CARD currently has NO sonnet-5 entry at all, only claude_sonnet_4_6 - that's a second, separate gap: the table itself needs a claude_sonnet_5 row before any normalizer can resolve to it)

**From this repo's own claude-api skill's authoritative pricing table (verified against skill content this session, current as of 2026-06-24):**
- claude-opus-4-8, claude-opus-4-7, claude-opus-4-6, claude-sonnet-5, claude-sonnet-4-6, claude-haiku-4-5, claude-fable-5, claude-mythos-5 (Project Glasswing only)

**Bare aliases (how a human/agent casually fills agent_create's provider.model field - observed convention in this repo's own agent definitions, e.g. env-adoption-analyst.md's `model: haiku`):**
- haiku, sonnet, opus, fable

**RATE_CARD's own current (mismatched, internally-inconsistent) key format - verified by reading pricing/rate-card.ts directly:**
- claude_sonnet_4_6, claude_opus_4_8, claude_haiku_4_5, claude_fable_5 (underscored)
- deepseek-v4-flash, deepseek-v4-pro (hyphenated - inconsistent with the Claude keys in the SAME table)

**Inferred by pattern, NOT individually live-verified this session - flag for confirmation before relying on:**
- Dated snapshot ids for other Claude models following the same `-YYYYMMDD` suffix pattern observed on haiku (e.g. a hypothetical claude-sonnet-5-20260615) - only the haiku variant was actually captured live.
- DeepSeek's real API-reported model id format (e.g. deepseek-chat / deepseek-reasoner style vs the versioned deepseek-v4-flash/-pro already in RATE_CARD) - not independently verified this session at all; whoever implements this should capture a real DeepSeek response before assuming a format.

**Negative-control sample (must still return null, per the existing 'never silently $0' rule):**
- totally-unrecognized-model-xyz (already covered by rate-card.test.ts's own existing test - keep it green through the refactor)

Also applies to usage-plugin.ts:108's separate model-resolution path (reads provider.model from the agent's own config, a DIFFERENT code path than usage.ts:584's info.usage.model) - both call sites should route through the same normalizer so they can never drift apart again.

